TA-hwraid
====

Collects hardware RAID controller state from storcli3/storcli (LSI/MegaRAID), ssacli (HP) or MegaCli, if a controller is present: controller state, drive counts, failed/rebuilding drives and cache/battery state. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype hwraid:status) and hwraid.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype hwraid:metrics). Hosts with no hardware RAID report 'absent' with a zero controller count, so fleet coverage stays visible.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * storcli3 (megaraid-sas / perccli) or ssacli (hpssacli) on hosts that have hardware RAID; auto-detected
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="hwraid:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="hwraid:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="hwraid.*" by host
  | mstats avg("hwraid.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=hwraid:status  (controller product, state, drive counts, battery)
Metrics: hwraid.controller_count / hwraid.c<n>_drive_count / hwraid.c<n>_failed_drives
Dashboards: TA-Hwraid > Hwraid Overview / Hwraid Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-hwraid/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * StorCLI must be executable by the Splunk service; it may need /dev/sg* access.
  * Software raid (md) is NOT covered here - see TA-zfspool.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-hwraid).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-hwraid/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
